    Research: CA-M delivery-age measurement amendment (oversight 1792107382)
    
    The watchdog's no_recent_main_commit signal measured only
    refs/remotes/origin/main, ignoring Kawun's active delivery line
    origin/release/along-long-namespace (128 commits ahead of main). This
    false-positived whenever work landed on the release line.
    
    oversight-watch.sh now takes the newest commit across origin/main and every
    origin/release/* ref for the threshold, with an optional bounded read-only
    fetch (VICHE_OVERSIGHT_FETCH=1, default off). Signal name and all
    incident/hearing/escalation semantics are unchanged. Adds
    local_delivery_commit_age_seconds alongside local_main_commit_age_seconds.
    
    Adds tests/oversight-release-signal-smoke.sh (POSIX /bin/sh): fresh release
    commit suppresses the false positive; idle repo (main+release stale) still
    triggers; main-only stale/fresh still behaves as before.
    
    Record: records/OVERSIGHT-CA-M-1792107382-research.md

